+From 86663a8236404b85f98789cb4cd7cb63da4a812e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: tomaszstaniak <nbw.designs@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:02:14 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 1/7] x86_64: add GOOS=aros and its thread-pointer lowering
+
+AROS has no ELF TLS and no syscalls, but the aros-tls kernel patch
+publishes the address of the running task's private word in the per-core
+block behind %gs, whose GDT descriptor is dpl=3 and so readable from
+userspace. That gives MOVQ TLS, r a one-load, call-free lowering.
+
+Since %gs:24 holds a pointer to the g slot rather than the slot itself,
+this is the two-instruction form, as on Plan 9 and Windows, and the
+linker's Tlsoffset is 0 because g sits at offset 0 of the block. The
+resulting g access assembles byte-identically to Plan 9's; only the base
+load differs, and needs no relocation.
+
+Toolchain only -- there is no runtime for this GOOS yet.
