+From 962070d7be0cb943244d073b87d36822c32f3aa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: tomaszstaniak <nbw.designs@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:13:52 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 3/7] runtime, cmd: stub the AROS OS layer and reach the
+ external linker
+
+Stubs with correct signatures for the 37 OS-layer symbols, deliberately
+throwing rather than working: the point is to compile and link a program
+so the -linkmode=external question can be answered before the real
+implementations are written, since a negative answer would change the
+shape of the port.
+
+lock_sema.go already supplies the note functions once aros is on its
+build tag, so those stubs came straight back out.
+
+Also: treat Haros as ELF in archinit and asmb2 so the linker writes a
+relocatable object for the host linker, but keep R_TLS_LE resolved
+internally -- g is reached through a pointer the kernel publishes in the
+%gs block, not through ELF TLS, so handing that relocation to
+x86_64-aros-gcc would ask it for something it cannot do. And drop -fPIC
+and -pthread for GOOS=aros in cmd/go, adding -mcmodel=large
+-mno-red-zone: AROS builds everything ET_REL and its gcc driver rejects
+-pthread outright.
+
+Everything now compiles, runtime/cgo included, and the linker reaches
+ELF relocation emission before failing on a size mismatch.
