++// AROS has POSIX threads (libpthread, one Exec task per thread) but no POSIX
++// signal masks: sigfillset and pthread_sigmask do not exist, because signals on
++// AROS are Exec's own per-task bits rather than Unix ones. So this is
++// pthread_unix.c with the mask dance removed. The stack-bound helper keeps the
++// pthread_getattr_np path, which AROS's pthread.h does provide.
