++// every thread ever created -- spinning on detached ones, joining the rest --
++// before the process is allowed to end. Its reason is sound (the code the
++// threads run is about to be unloaded), but a Go M parked in semasleep never
++// returns on its own, so a plain exit() would wait forever. Measured: it does.
++//
